(A quiet hour) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Every evening, Maya sets aside a quiet hour to read. She chooses a) Tj
T*
(short article, puts her phone on a stand, and opens her notebook. Her) Tj
T*
(aim is not to finish as quickly as possible. She wants to understand) Tj
T*
(how each idea connects to the next. When a word is unfamiliar, she) Tj
T*
(first looks at the surrounding sentence. Sometimes the meaning becomes) Tj
T*
(clear without a dictionary.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(At other times, Maya saves a small note in Chinese beside the word.) Tj
T*
(The note records the meaning that fits this particular passage. A) Tj
T*
(familiar word may have a different meaning in another context, so she) Tj
T*
(does not treat every definition as a rule. She reads the paragraph) Tj
T*
(again, checks the original page when necessary, and changes her note) Tj
T*
(if her understanding improves.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(At the end of the hour, she exports a few useful words together with) Tj
T*
(their original sentences. The next morning she hides the Chinese notes) Tj
T*
(and reads the passage once more. This simple routine turns a list of) Tj
T*
(isolated words into a record of ideas she has understood.) Tj
T*
() Tj
